Here is a basic React component that provides autocomplete functionality without relying on third-party packages:
```
import React, { useState } from 'react';

const Autocomplete = ({ labelText, suggestions, onSelect }) => {
  const [query, setQuery] = useState('');
  const [activeSuggestion, setActiveSuggestion] = useState(null);
  const [suggestionsList, setSuggestionsList] = useState([]);

  const handleInputChange = (e) => {
    setQuery(e.target.value);
  };

  const handleSuggestionsListShow = () => {
    setSuggestionsList(query
      ? suggestions.filter((suggestion) => suggestion.toLowerCase().includes(query.toLowerCase()))
      : []);
    setActiveSuggestion(null);
  };

  const handleSuggestionsListHide = () => {
    setSuggestionsList([]);
    setActiveSuggestion(null);
  };

  const handleOnArrowUp = () => {
    if (activeSuggestion === null) return;
    const prevSuggestion = activeSuggestion - 1;
    if (prevSuggestion < 0) return;
    setActiveSuggestion(prevSuggestion);
  };

  const handleOnArrowDown = () => {
    if (activeSuggestion === null) return;
    const nextSuggestion = activeSuggestion + 1;
    if (nextSuggestion >= suggestionsList.length) return;
    setActiveSuggestion(nextSuggestion);
  };

  const handleEnter = () => {
    if (activeSuggestion === null) return;
    onSelect(suggestionsList[activeSuggestion]);
  };

  const handleSuggestionSelect = (suggestion) => {
    onSelect(suggestion);
    setQuery '';
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <label>{labelText}</label>
      <input
        type="text"
        value={query}
        onChange={handleInputChange}
        onFocus={handleSuggestionsListShow}
        onBlur={handleSuggestionsListHide}
      />
      <ul>
        {suggestionsList.map((suggestion, index) => (
          <li
            key={suggestion}
            className={activeSuggestion === index ? 'active' : ''}
            onClick={() => handleSuggestionSelect(suggestion)}
          >
            {suggestion}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <div
        className="arrow-up"
        tabIndex="-1"
        onClick={handleOnArrowUp}
      />
      <div
        className="arrow-down"
        tabIndex="-1"
        onClick={handleOnArrowDown}
      />
      <div
        className="enter"
        tabIndex="-1"
        onClick={handleEnter}
      />
    </div>
  );
};

export default Autocomplete;
```
This component takes three props:

* `labelText`: the text to display as the label for the autocomplete input
* `suggestions`: an array of strings that the user can choose from
* `onSelect`: a function to call when the user selects a suggestion

The component uses three states:

* `query`: the current value of the autocomplete input
* `activeSuggestion`: the index of the currently highlighted suggestion
* `suggestionsList`: an array of suggestions that match the user's query

The component has several event handlers:

* `handleInputChange`: updates the `query` state when the user types something
* `handleSuggestionsListShow`: updates the `suggestionsList` state when the user focuses on the input
* `handleSuggestionsListHide`: updates the `suggestionsList` state when the user blurs the input
